  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let\n\n\\[ \\frac{35x-29}{x^2-3x+2} =\\frac{N_1}{x-1}+\\frac{N_2}{x-2} \\]\n\nbe an identity in \\(x.\\) The numerical value of \\(N_1N_2\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-246\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-210\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-29\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(210\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(246\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
