    "value": "-246"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Combining the right side gives numerator \\[ \\begin{aligned} &N_1(x-2)+N_2(x-1)\\\\ &\\quad=(N_1+N_2)x\\\\ &\\qquad-(2N_1+N_2). \\end{aligned} \\] Thus \\(N_1+N_2=35\\) and \\(2N_1+N_2=29.\\) Hence \\(N_1=-6,\\) \\(N_2=41,\\) and \\(N_1N_2=-246.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the two fractions over \\((x-1)(x-2)\\)",
        "Compare the coefficient of \\(x\\) and the constant term"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
